{#
  Rendered byte-for-byte as the live drop-in on the vps host (installed there
  on 2026-10-02 by vps-info services/ssh-hardening/install.sh, the approved
  design). The first comment line still names that installer ON PURPOSE: any
  change to the rendered bytes is a change the role must apply and a reload it
  must perform, so rewording it is a deliberate follow-up, not a side effect.

  The 00- prefix is load-bearing: sshd takes the FIRST value it obtains for
  each keyword and the Include glob expands lexically, so this file must sort
  ahead of cloud-init's 50- drop-in, which sets PasswordAuthentication.
#}
# Managed by vps-info/services/ssh-hardening/install.sh.
# Public IPv4 only; Tailscale SSH owns incoming tailnet port 22 independently.
# The 00- prefix takes precedence over Ubuntu cloud-init defaults.
ListenAddress {{ ssh_hardening_public_address }}:{{ ssh_hardening_port }}
PasswordAuthentication no
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
PermitRootLogin prohibit-password
PermitEmptyPasswords no
PubkeyAuthentication yes
MaxAuthTries {{ ssh_hardening_max_auth_tries }}
LoginGraceTime {{ ssh_hardening_login_grace_time }}
MaxStartups {{ ssh_hardening_max_startups }}
